.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt RTWB 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rtwb
.Nd native driver for the Realtek RTL8822BE IEEE 802.11ac wireless adapter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
The driver is not loaded automatically, because the base system's
.Xr rtw88 4
driver claims the same device.
To use
.Nm
instead, place the following lines in
.Xr rc.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
devmatch_blocklist="${devmatch_blocklist} if_rtw88"
kld_list="${kld_list} if_rtwb"
.Ed
.Pp
To load the driver by hand:
.Pp
.Dl kldload if_rtwb
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides support for the Realtek RTL8822BE PCIe wireless network
adapter on top of the native
.Xr net80211 4
wireless stack.
It does not use the
.Xr linuxkpi 4
compatibility framework.
The hardware support code is ported from Realtek's rtw88 driver for
Linux.
.Pp
The driver supports station and monitor mode.
It supports IEEE 802.11a/b/g, 802.11n with 20 and 40 MHz channels, and
802.11ac with 80 MHz channels, with two spatial streams.
Transmit rates are chosen by the adapter's firmware.
WEP, TKIP and CCMP are done in software by
.Xr net80211 4 .
Only one virtual interface can exist at a time.
.Pp
The driver needs the RTL8822B firmware image
.Pa rtw88/rtw8822b_fw.bin ,
which is loaded with
.Xr firmware 9 .
It is provided by the
.Pa net/wifi-firmware-rtw88-kmod@rtw8822b
port
.Pq package Pa wifi-firmware-rtw88-kmod-rtw8822b .
.Pp
For more information on configuring this device, see
.Xr ifconfig 8 .
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the following PCIe Wi-Fi devices:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset indent -compact
.It
Realtek 802.11ac wireless 8822be (RTL8822BE)
.El
.Pp
It has been tested on a Lenovo ThinkPad A475 only (RFE option 5,
Bluetooth antenna shared with Wi-Fi).
The attach message shows the RFE option and the antenna sharing of a
board.
Boards are wired differently, and the Wi-Fi/Bluetooth coexistence setup
may need tuning on other RFE options.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following read-only variables report driver statistics under
.Va dev.rtwb.%d :
.Bl -tag -width "tx_err_map_last"
.It Va rx_frames , rx_beacons , rx_crc_err
Frames received, beacons received, and frames dropped because of a CRC
or ICV error.
.It Va rx_tag_err
Receive descriptors whose sequence tag did not match; the first one is
reported as
.Dq pci bus timeout, check dma status .
.It Va tx_frames , tx_done
Frames handed to the hardware and frames the hardware completed.
.It Va tx_queued
Frames that waited in the driver's send queue for a free descriptor.
.It Va tx_qfull
Frames dropped because the send queue was full.
.It Va tx_err , tx_err_encap , tx_err_mbuf , tx_err_map , tx_err_map_last
Frames dropped because of an error, split by cause: crypto
encapsulation, mbuf allocation, DMA mapping, and the error number of the
last DMA mapping failure.
.It Va ra_rate , ra_bw , ra_reports
The rate and channel width last chosen by the firmware's rate adaptation,
and the number of its reports.
.It Va txpwr
The transmit power index programmed for each rate and RF path.
.It Va intr , rx_c2h , h2c_sent , h2c_done , last_c2h_id
Interrupt and firmware message counters.
.El
.Pp
The following variables are writable and meant for debugging:
.Bl -tag -width "tx_err_map_last"
.It Va debug
Print the rate adaptation parameters on association.
.It Va tx_report
Ask the firmware to report the outcome of every transmitted frame;
counted in
.Va tx_rpt_ok
and
.Va tx_rpt_fail .
.It Va reg_addr , reg_val
Read or write the 32-bit chip register at
.Va reg_addr .
.It Va channel
Tune the radio to a 20 MHz channel, bypassing
.Xr net80211 4 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/boot/firmware/rtw88/rtw8822b_fw.bin" -compact
.It Pa /boot/modules/if_rtwb.ko
The driver module.
.It Pa /boot/firmware/rtw88/rtw8822b_fw.bin
The firmware image.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Join a WPA2 network at boot, with the regulatory country set to New
Zealand, in
.Xr rc.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wlans_rtwb0="wlan0"
create_args_wlan0="country NZ"
ifconfig_wlan0="WPA DHCP"
.Ed
.Pp
Replace the station interface with a monitor mode interface and capture
frames with their radio information:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ifconfig wlan0 destroy
ifconfig wlan0 create wlandev rtwb0 wlanmode monitor up
tcpdump -i wlan0 -y IEEE802_11_RADIO
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "rtwb%d: could not load firmware rtw88/rtw8822b_fw.bin"
The firmware package is not installed.
.It "rtwb%d: unsupported RFE option %u"
The board uses a radio front-end layout the driver does not know.
.It "rtwb%d: hardware init failed (%d)"
The adapter could not be brought up when the interface was marked up.
.El
