.Sh CAVEATS
The RTL8822BE shares its antenna with the Bluetooth part of the chip.
The driver programs a static arbitration setup: while a
.Nm
interface is up, the chip's arbiter shares the antenna, which is enough
for light traffic such as a mouse or a keyboard, including devices that
reconnect on their own; while the interface is down, Bluetooth owns the
antenna.
During heavy 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi traffic some incoming Bluetooth connection
attempts fail and the device has to retry.
Bluetooth audio together with 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi may suffer; if it does, use
5 GHz or bring the interface down.
.Pp
The regulatory database
.Pa /etc/regdomain.xml
has no 802.11ac channels for some regions.
If
.Xr net80211 4
then falls back to 802.11a on 5 GHz, add
.Cm -vht
to the interface's creation arguments to use 802.11n instead.
.Sh BUGS
The driver does not do transmit A-MPDU aggregation, hardware crypto,
power saving, or beamforming.
.Pp
The bpf parameters of injected frames (rate, retries) are ignored.
